%S A402567 1,3,1,5,2,1,7,1,3,2,1,10,3,6,3,1,2,1,14,5,8,1,5,2,3,1,2,18,8,10,2,7,
%T A402567 3,5,4,4,21,11,12,5,10,4,6,5,6,27,14,13,8,12,7,9,7,1,7,32,17,16,9,13,
%U A402567 9,13,8,4,8,37,18,20,11,14,10,15,12,5,11,47,21
%N A402567 Positive counts read successively from the decimal self-stirring word: start with 1, cycle through labels 0,...,9, skip zero counts, otherwise append the current count followed by its label, updating all counts immediately.
%H A402567 Lei Zhou (SWUST), <a href="/A402567/b402567.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A402567 Lei Zhou, <a href="https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202610.1633/v2">Self-Stirring Sequences: Exact Dynamics and Statistical Rigidity</a>, Preprints.org, version 2, November 19, 2026.
%F A402567 a(n) ~ n*log_10(n)/10. After finitely many rounds all ten labels are active. At round r each label has count asymptotic to r*log_10(r), and its count changes by O(log(r)) within the round. See Zhou, Theorems 2.6 and 2.7.
%e A402567 Round 1 reads the single positive count 1 (label 1). Round 2 reads 3 at label 1 and 1 at label 3. Round 3 reads 5, 2, 1 at labels 1, 3, 5. Thus the sequence starts 1,3,1,5,2,1. The skipped zero counts are not terms.
%o A402567 (Python)
%o A402567 def terms():
%o A402567     c = [0]*10
%o A402567     c[1] = 1
%o A402567     while True:
%o A402567         for d in range(10):
%o A402567             q = c[d]
%o A402567             if q:
%o A402567                 for x in list(map(int, str(q))) + [d]:
%o A402567                     c[x] += 1
%o A402567                 yield q
%Y A402567 Cf. A402566 (digit stream), A402568 (lengths after complete rounds).
%K A402567 nonn,base,easy,new
%O A402567 1,2
%A A402567 _Lei Zhou (SWUST)_, Nov 21 2026
